    The behaviours that only a real database can demonstrate: SKIP LOCKED, unique
    indexes deciding a race, JSONB round trips and optimistic concurrency. An
    in-memory provider agrees with whatever the code does, which is precisely why
    it cannot answer any of these.

    Everything here carries Category=Integration, so the ordinary CI run skips it
    and a machine without a Docker daemon is not blocked.
  -->

